title: Education & Science
new-page: true
is-card: true
view-if: spd_in_government and spd_states and chancellor_party = "SPD" and education_science_timer = 0 and (recession_seen = 0 or return_to_normalcy = 1)
on-arrival: education_science_timer += 9; month_actions += 1
card-image: img/portraits/EinsteinAlbert.jpg
go-to: ed_menu
tags: govt_affairs, cabinet

= Education and Science

Schools are the business of the Länder, but the federal government pays for much of what matters: the digital pact, all-day schools, student grants and research. With the chancellery and our Länder governments, we can shape policy for a large part of the country.

[? if major_curriculum: Current focus of the curriculum: [+ major_curriculum +], [+ minor_curriculum +] ?]

@ed_menu
view-if: not last_advisor_action

- @increase_science
- @structure
- @curriculum
- @return: Do not enact any policies for now.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@increase_science
title: Increase funding for research.
choose-if: economic_minister_party = "SPD"
unavailable-subtitle: This requires the economics ministry.

German research is still among the best in the world, but it is falling behind the United States and China in the technologies that will decide the coming decades. What should we fund?

- @kwg
- @applied
- @medical
- @cut_funding
- @ed_menu: Do not increase research funding.
- @cancel_advisor_action

@kwg
title: Fund basic research at the Max Planck Society and the universities.
subtitle: -1 budget
choose-if: budget >= 1
on-arrival: budget -= 1; science += 1; kwg_research += 1; economic_growth += 0.1; new_middle_spd += 4*(1-dissent); greens_relation += 4*(1-dissent); west_relation += 1; science_funding += 1

We fund new research groups and bring back researchers who left for America, including scientists fleeing political pressure on American universities.

@applied
title: Fund applied research in key technologies.
subtitle: -1 budget
choose-if: budget >= 1
on-arrival: budget -= 1; science += 1; applied_research += 1; economic_growth += 0.2; economic_growth += 0.1 if applied_research > 1; new_middle_spd += 4*(1-dissent); workers_spd += 2*(1-dissent); greens_relation += 3*(1-dissent); unemployment_rate -= 0.1 if unemployment_rate >= 4; capital_strike_progress -= 1 if capital_strike_progress > 1; science_funding += 1

We fund research on AI, chips, batteries and hydrogen with the Fraunhofer institutes and industry, so that the jobs of the future are created in Germany.

@medical
title: Fund medical research and public health.
subtitle: -1 budget
choose-if: budget >= 1
on-arrival: budget -= 1; science += 1; medical_research += 1; economic_growth += 0.1; new_middle_spd += 3*(1-dissent); workers_spd += 2*(1-dissent); pensioners_spd += 2*(1-dissent); greens_relation += 3*(1-dissent); science_funding += 1

We fund research on cancer, dementia and pandemics in the university hospitals.

@cut_funding
title: Cut research funding.
subtitle: +1 budget
choose-if: science_funding >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have not increased research funding.
on-arrival: budget += 1; science -= 1; science_funding -= 1; applied_research -= 0.33; kwg_research -= 0.33; medical_research -= 0.33; economic_growth -= 0.2; new_middle_spd -= 4; workers_spd -= 1; greens_relation -= 4

We cut research funding. The universities protest, and some researchers leave for Switzerland and the Netherlands.

@structure
title: Change the structure and funding of schools.

No country in the OECD ties school success as closely to the parents' income as Germany. Children are sorted into different school types at the age of ten, many schools are falling apart, and there are not enough teachers.

- @secularize
- @public_hs
- @school_boards
- @ed_menu: Do not change school funding or organisation.
- @cancel_advisor_action

@secularize
title: Replace confessional religious education with a common ethics and religions class.
subtitle: -1 budget
unavailable-subtitle: -1 budget. This needs a majority of parties in favour.
choose-if: budget >= 1 and (progressive_coalition + fdp_r >= 50)
view-if: secularized = 0

Are you sure about this? The churches and the Union will fight it hard. [? if cdu_in_government : Our coalition partners may well walk out. ?]

- @secularize_2: Yes, do it.
- @ed_menu: No, leave religious education as it is.
- @cancel_advisor_action

@secularize_2
on-arrival: secularized = 1; rural_spd -= 4; pensioners_spd -= 2; catholics_spd += 2*(1-dissent); cdu_relation -= 12; coalition_dissent += 2 if cdu_in_government; fdp_relation += 4*(1-dissent); greens_relation += 4*(1-dissent); linke_relation += 4*(1-dissent); new_middle_spd += 3*(1-dissent); workers_spd += 2*(1-dissent); education_science += 0.5

With the Grüne, the FDP and the Linke, our Länder bring in a common class on ethics and world religions, as Berlin has had since 2006. The churches and the Union are outraged.

@public_hs
title: Fund longer learning together and schools in poor neighbourhoods.
subtitle: -1 budget
choose-if: budget >= 1
on-arrival: budget -= 1; public_hs += 1; workers_spd += 5*(1-dissent); unemployed_spd += 3*(1-dissent); federal_police_loyalty += 0.02; education_science += 0.5; unemployment_rate -= 0.1; economic_growth += 0.1; trust_in_democracy += 3*(1-dissent);
max-visits: 3

We fund more teachers, social workers and free lunches in schools in poor areas, and support Länder that keep children together until the age of twelve.

@school_boards
title: Give parents and pupils more say in their schools.
on-arrival: school_boards += 1; workers_spd += 2*(1-dissent); new_middle_spd += 3*(1-dissent); old_middle_spd += 2*(1-dissent); education_science += 0.2;
view-if: school_boards = 0

Schools get their own budgets, and parents and pupils get a real say in how they are spent.

@curriculum
title: Change the educational curriculum.
choose-if: curriculum_timer = 0
unavailable-subtitle: [? if curriculum_timer > 0 : It is too early to change the curriculum again. ?]

Through the conference of education ministers, our Länder can agree on common standards for what schools should teach. Pupils' results in reading and mathematics have been falling for a decade.

What should be the major focus of our new curriculum?

- @dem_major
- @science_major
- @human_major
- @vocational_major
- @trad_major
- @ed_menu: Do not change the curriculum now.
- @cancel_advisor_action

# note: education_science is a variable that affects how much education affects economic growth.

@dem_major
title: Democratic curriculum
subtitle: Critical thinking, democratic citizenship, and collaboration
on-arrival: curriculum_timer = 50; major_curriculum = "democratic"; trust_in_democracy += 5*(1-dissent); workers_spd += 3*(1-dissent); democratization += 1; cdu_relation -= 3; fdp_relation -= 5; coalition_dissent += 1 if in_grand_coalition; pacifism += 1; education_science += 0.3
go-to: curriculum_minor

Pupils should learn how democracy works, how to spot disinformation online, and how to argue and disagree with respect. Conservatives say that schools should teach knowledge, not politics.

@science_major
title: Scientific curriculum
subtitle: Mathematics, science, computing and technical skills
on-arrival: curriculum_timer = 50; major_curriculum = "scientific"; education_science += 1; coalition_dissent += 1 if in_weimar_coalition; cdu_relation -= 5; greens_relation += 4*(1-dissent); linke_relation += 3*(1-dissent); new_middle_spd += 3*(1-dissent); workers_spd += 2*(1-dissent)
go-to: curriculum_minor

Our schools should prepare pupils for a digital economy, with more mathematics, science and computing. 

@human_major
title: Humanist curriculum
subtitle: Arts, literature, history, and philosophy
on-arrival: curriculum_timer = 50; major_curriculum = "humanist"; greens_relation += 3*(1-dissent); new_middle_spd += 4*(1-dissent); education_science += 0.2
go-to: curriculum_minor

Our educational curriculum should be focused on the humanities, including arts, literature, history, and philosophy. Some criticise this as a focus on "useless" subjects.

@vocational_major
title: Vocational curriculum
subtitle: Practical skills and a better path into apprenticeships
on-arrival: curriculum_timer = 50; major_curriculum = "vocational"; fdp_relation += 3*(1-dissent); greens_relation += 3*(1-dissent); workers_spd += 4*(1-dissent); rural_spd += 2*(1-dissent); unemployed_spd += 3*(1-dissent); new_middle_spd -= 1; unemployment_rate -= 0.1; education_science += 0.5
go-to: curriculum_minor

Schools should prepare pupils better for an apprenticeship, with more practical work and closer ties to local employers.


@trad_major
title: Traditional curriculum
subtitle: Discipline, the classics and German identity
on-arrival: curriculum_timer = 50; major_curriculum = "traditional"; fdp_relation += 5*(1-dissent); cdu_relation += 4*(1-dissent); old_middle_spd += 3*(1-dissent); rural_spd += 3*(1-dissent); pacifism -= 1 if pacifism > 0; trust_in_democracy -= 5; education_science += 0.2
go-to: curriculum_minor

A return to grades from the first year, strict discipline, the classics and a stronger focus on German history and identity, as the Union has demanded.


@curriculum_minor

And what should be a secondary focus of the curriculum?

- @dem_minor
- @science_minor
- @human_minor
- @vocational_minor
- @trad_minor

@dem_minor
title: Democratic curriculum
subtitle: Critical thinking, democratic citizenship, and collaboration
view-if: major_curriculum != "democratic"
on-arrival: minor_curriculum = "democratic"; trust_in_democracy += 3*(1-dissent); workers_spd += 2*(1-dissent); democratization += 1; cdu_relation -= 2; fdp_relation -= 3;

Pupils should learn how democracy works, how to spot disinformation online, and how to argue and disagree with respect. Conservatives say that schools should teach knowledge, not politics.

@science_minor
title: Scientific curriculum
subtitle: Mathematics, science, computing and technical skills
view-if: major_curriculum != "scientific"
on-arrival: minor_curriculum = "scientific"; education_science += 0.5; cdu_relation -= 3; greens_relation += 3*(1-dissent); linke_relation += 2*(1-dissent); new_middle_spd += 2*(1-dissent); workers_spd += 2*(1-dissent)

Our schools should prepare pupils for a digital economy, with more mathematics, science and computing. 

@human_minor
title: Humanist curriculum
subtitle: Arts, literature, history, and philosophy
view-if: major_curriculum != "humanist"
on-arrival: minor_curriculum = "humanist"; new_middle_spd += 3*(1-dissent); greens_relation += 3*(1-dissent);

Our educational curriculum should be focused on the humanities, including arts, literature, history, and philosophy. Some criticise this as a focus on "useless" subjects.

@vocational_minor
title: Vocational curriculum
subtitle: Practical skills and a better path into apprenticeships
view-if: major_curriculum != "vocational"
on-arrival: minor_curriculum = "vocational"; education_science += 0.3; workers_spd += 3*(1-dissent); unemployed_spd += 2*(1-dissent);

Schools should prepare pupils better for an apprenticeship, with more practical work and closer ties to local employers.


@trad_minor
title: Traditional curriculum
subtitle: Discipline, the classics and German identity
view-if: major_curriculum != "traditional"
on-arrival: minor_curriculum = "traditional"; fdp_relation += 2*(1-dissent); cdu_relation += 2*(1-dissent); old_middle_spd += 2*(1-dissent); rural_spd += 2*(1-dissent); trust_in_democracy -= 3

A return to strict discipline, the classics and a stronger focus on German identity.


